1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Chén Bówèi 陳伯位 [Bâk Vì] was the second son of 陳耀馨 Chén Yàoxīn [Yèl Hëng]. His tomb was in Zhīnǚwān 織女灣 [Jēik Nuī Vön] in the shape of a beautiful girl tossing her comb away facing east. He was buried next to Chén Y
2 CONC àozhāng 陳耀章 [Yèl Jëng] (his uncle from the Chén Zhònglún 陳仲倫 [Jùng Lũn] branch) and Chén Bóhuī 陳伯徽 [Bâk Fï] (his cousin). He married a woman from the Tán 譚 [Hâm] family. Her tomb was in  Pàobù Dìmiànhē 泡步地面喝 [Päo Bǔ Ì Mèin Höt] in
2 CONC  the shape of a cat facing north. He had three sons, Chén Cháobīn 陳朝賓 [Chẽl Bïn], Chén Cháozhù 陳朝苧 [Chẽl Chuî], and Chén Cháozōng 陳朝宗 [Chẽl Düng].
