1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Following his father's footsteps Chen Bon Sim placed first in the provincial imperial examinations in 1714. Together Chin Bon Sim and his father established the Cha Zhou (台山六村槎州村) branch of the Chen family. He had 
2 CONC ten sons.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note on Generation Numbers (145, 137, 104, 22, 18世)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Bon Sim is a 145th generation descendant of Huang Di (the Yellow Emperor) (2,697-2,597 BC), and following the patrilineal line of descent:
2 CONT * a 137th generation descendant of Gui Shun Di, 媯舜帝, 9,1G (2,305-2,205 BC)
2 CONT * a 104th generation descendant of Chén Hú Gōng 陳胡公, 42, 34,1G the first ruler of the Chen Kingdom
2 CONT * a 22th generation descendant of Chén Xuān 陳宣 (1174-1256) who established the 石頭新會 (Stone Village, Xin Hui, Guangdong, China) branch of the family
2 CONT * a 18th generation descendant of Chén Tiānxiáng 裔昌/從善/天祥, 128,120,87,40,5,1G who established the 上閣東山台山縣 (Shangge, Dongshan, Taishan County, Guangdong, China) branch of the family.
1 FAMC @F6000000026909666898@
1 FAMS @F6000000026783520669@
1 FAMS @F6000000026784413172@
1 RFN geni:6000000026783520664
1 SUBM @S6000000002920088413@
1 OBJE
2 FILE https://media.geni.com/p13/cc/4c/2b/34/5344483c43406a9f/nuv65yac_original.jpg?hash=4fad1f0f1c0cd6fd060c49557e7d15e8a64845c5cea66570e90c1afd5f4bf797.1797235199
2 FORM jpg
2 TITL Ten sons of Chén Hàn/Běn Shēn/Chǔ Xià (陳瀚/本深/处下). 
2 _PRIM Y
2 NOTE Ken,
3 CONT
3 CONT I suggest the title for your maternal pedigree chart to read as “Guangdong First Ancestor Chen Fengtai to Chen Zhao Fan (Chin Sui Fan) Descendants in US” (廣東始祖陳鳳臺至美國陳肇蕃裔).
3 CONT
3 CONT The dates of birth and death for your maternal ancestors are provided in your Jiapu. I normally would indicate the year of birth and death of each ancestor at sides of the chart.  If you wish to include them, I suppose you are abl
3 CONC e to convert the dates given therein into Gregorian dates. If you can do that, it would save me sometime in extracting the information from the related profiles in your jiapu to convert them.
3 CONT
3 CONT There are interesting commentaries and/or family histories for some of your maternal ancestors provided in the jiapu. If you can get them translated, it would be interesting to include them as well.
3 CONT
3 CONT If the generation names are given in the jiapu, you may wish to include them as well.  If it is in the form of a poem, you could get it translated and include it and the translation into the chart.
3 CONT
3 CONT You may have family photos than you may wish to include them in the chart.
3 CONT
3 CONT If you know the movements of your ancestors from one place to another you may wish to provide a map showing such movements and indicating the generations that stayed in each place.   
3 CONT
3 CONT From maternal side you would be my 50th cousin 7 times removed.  The common ancestor is Jīn Gōng (Kuāng)[ 津公(匡)] at Generation  94,86,53,6.
3 CONT
3 CONT Philip
2 NOTE I'm looking at it now. Thank you!
2 NOTE Ken,
3 CONT Sent you the first draft a while ago.
3 CONT
3 CONT Philip
2 NOTE Ken,
3 CONT
3 CONT OK, I shall do it for you based upon what you had enter in Geni.com.  On seeing the first draft, things can easily be changed to suit. Consider the photos you want to add; besides those of individual profiles.
3 CONT
3 CONT Philip
2 NOTE Philip,
3 CONT I was planning to fill in the chart to my family, but if you have an easy way to do that, I'd be very thankful.
3 CONT Cheers,
3 CONT Ken
2 NOTE Hi Ken,
3 CONT
3 CONT OK I shall send you the excel file when I get back home tonight. I am out having meetings the whole day. Do you want me to fill up the file down to your family first? I could easily do that for you. The form of the chart as you sa
3 CONC w is for the Forum. 
3 CONT
3 CONT I shall include the adoption side as well.
3 CONT
3 CONT Philip
2 NOTE Uncle Philip, you're the same generation as the 10 sons of Chen Han, and our relationship path is now much closer now that I've connected my mother's family to the the world family tree.
2 NOTE If you save the file in PDF format, people will be able to click on the links you've provided.
2 NOTE Hi Philip, this chart is great. Could you send me the excel file?  Also this chart overlaps with Dore's chart through Chén Huī 陳輝 136, 128, 95, 48, 13, 9世.  There are a couple of adoptions reflected in Dore's chart that aren't her
3 CONC e (starting at Xin 信, 133,125,92,45,10,6 and going through Liangzuo 良佐, 135,127,94,47,12,8).
