1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "The third son, your grandfather, past the Ching Dynasty examination
2 CONT
2 CONT for government service, but unfortunately the Ching Dynasty was abolished by
2 CONT
2 CONT the revolution. Your grandfather was then came to the US to study. What,
2 CONT
2 CONT where, how long, and means of support is sketchy since the KMT government
2 CONT
2 CONT finance is not in good standing at that time. Your Dad came to the US in 1927"  
2 CONT
2 CONT   - John Ng
2 CONT
2 CONT The elder brothers probably sent a lot of money back to support somebody successful in school. Apparently scholars were quite pampered then. He had a servant who took care of him in student quarters. Mom Sui Ying, Amy and I may ha
2 CONC ve met that servant when we visited the village in 1994. Yin Ai was not very enthusiastic about his early marriage, and fathered two sons just before leaving for the USA. 
2 CONT
2 CONT As we heard it from our father Are Shing, he studied Journalism for a while at a prestigious college, probably Harvard, until the scholarship was suspended. From there, joined friends in San Francisco for a while, then ended up wo
2 CONC rking in a grocery store in Shelby Mississippi. He sent for his eldest son, my father,  who was then 16, and settled him in Chicago with restaurant friends.   Yin Ai came down with typhoid six months later and Are Shing brought hi
2 CONC m up to Chicago for treatment. The Chinese treatment of scraping the skin did not succeed, and he passed away in the basement of the restaurant building which was then on the corner or 47th and Prairie.
