1 NOTE {geni:about_me} At age 16, came to the US in 1927, lived in Ft. Shelby, Mississippi until his father died six months later. Joined relatives to work in the South Side Chicago restaurant which he eventually owned until his passing 
2 CONC in 1973. It is said his first marriage to a Chinese Anerican ended in divorce. He served in China in World War II, which resulted in gaining both citizenship and the privilege of importing a War Bride, my mother Sui Ying.  
