1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Younger brother to Are Shing Chan. Are Shing helped arrange for Park to come to the USA in 1939. Brother Are Shing Chan at age 16, came to the US in 1925, lived in Ft. Shelby, Mississippi until his father died six 
2 CONC months later. Later Park Shing Chan joined his brother to work in the South Side Chicago, ILL restaurant at 47th street next to the "L" station around 1960's. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Park was born May 5, 1911 (recorded May 5, 1907) and he passed away  May 30, 1998 at the age of 87 (91). His first marriage was to Yee Won Lee Chan and second marriage to Yuet Chan (both deceased now.) His married name was spelled
2 CONC  Chin Nai Din according to immigration records.
2 CONT
2 CONT He served in Europe during World War II as a Sgt - Short Order Cook. Earned American Theater Ribbon, European African Middle Eastern Theater Ribbon w/4 Bronze Battle Stars, 4 Overseas Sevice Bars, 1 Sevice Stripe and Good Conduct 
2 CONC Metal (GO 9 200 Sig 44). He enlisted in the Army on Feb 23, 1942 at Camp Grant, Illinois went to England Oct 20, 1943, D-Day June 6, 1944 Normandy, Northern France, Rhineland, Central Europe and back to the USA on Oct 12, 1945. He
2 CONC  was then honorably discharged at Fort Sheridan, Illinois in Oct 27, 1945 which resulted in gaining both citizenship and permission to bring his family to the USA. Subsequently, wife Yee Won Lee Chan and his daughter Mai Mai Chan 
2 CONC entered the USA sometime after 1946. They were prevented by the pre-war Chinese Exclusion laws.
