1 NOTE {geni:about_me} G. I. Prayer
2 CONT
2 CONT Written by F. S. Chin
2 CONT
2 CONT Somewhere in China, 1946
2 CONT
2 CONT Found on March 3, 1985 
2 CONT
2 CONT Please God, please remember us.
2 CONT
2 CONT We are the ones that were in Saipan.
2 CONT
2 CONT We are the ones that were on the beach of Normandy.
2 CONT
2 CONT We are the ones in Okinawa, Burma, India, and China.
2 CONT
2 CONT We are the ones in the far reaches of all the world.
2 CONT
2 CONT When our souls were on trial there, we looked up to you.
2 CONT
2 CONT And your smile came; we were assured, we came through.
2 CONT
2 CONT People say we have won,
2 CONT
2 CONT But you know what we have done, don't you?
2 CONT
2 CONT Today in this quiet moment of gratitude once more we are on trial.
2 CONT
2 CONT Once more we look up and ask your guidance.
2 CONT
2 CONT We ask nothing of you - nothing, O Lord, nothing save this!
2 CONT
2 CONT Please smile again. Please remember us
2 CONT
2 CONT In peace as you did so dearly in war. Amen. 
